aL8(a){return"Volatility: measures how much your portfolio value swings day to day, expressed as an annualised percentage.\n\nSharpe Ratio: how much return you're earning per unit of risk taken, after subtracting a risk-free baseline. Higher is better. A ratio of 1.0 means you earn 1% of excess return per 1% of annual volatility.\n\nBoth use your actual recorded portfolio values \u2014 no theoretical assumptions about holdings."+a},
